  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159634",
      "title": "Adding Another Route via the File System",
      "lectureOrder": 88,
      "videoOrder": 82,
      "sourceHash": "a488889d0bf1dadb9f4f6e000e99230a858ccdfb63a4c3446863b0de9bbe6dcd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "So NextJS has these server components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 7.32,
          "en": "components that are rendered and converted to HTML,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.32,
          "end": 9.033,
          "en": "which is then sent to the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.99,
          "end": 12.63,
          "en": "And as I mentioned, the file name here matters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.63,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "because it's that file name that tells NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.63,
          "end": 17.883,
          "en": "that we want to have this as a page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.99,
          "end": 22.56,
          "en": "But how could we now add a second page to this website?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.56,
          "end": 24.51,
          "en": "Let's say we also want to be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.51,
          "end": 28.773,
          "en": "to reach a page, localhost:3000/about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.94,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "If that is what we want to do, we have to find some way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 37.473,
          "en": "of letting NextJS know about our intentions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.55,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "Now, if we were using just React without NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.15,
          "end": 44.313,
          "en": "we could use React Router for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.11,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "But in NextJS projects, you don't do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "Instead here, this app directory plays an important role",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "because in this app directory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 60.5,
          "en": "you can add new paths, which you wanna handle as routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.08,
          "end": 63.6,
          "en": "by adding new folders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.6,
          "end": 67.47,
          "en": "So if we want to support a /about route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.47,
          "end": 69.873,
          "en": "we have to add an about folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 75.33,
          "en": "However, on its own, this folder won't do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.33,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "If I just add this folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 80.16,
          "en": "and I then go to /about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.16,
          "end": 83.313,
          "en": "I get this default 404 page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.66,
          "end": 85.86,
          "en": "and I'm getting this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.86,
          "end": 90.42,
          "en": "because NextJS doesn't know about this about route yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.42,
          "end": 92.523,
          "en": "adding a folder is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.72,
          "end": 97.89,
          "en": "Instead, you always also must add such a page.JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.89,
          "end": 100.65,
          "en": "if you want to render a page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.65,
          "end": 103.233,
          "en": "which kind of makes sense, I guess.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.55,
          "en": "So now we don't just have that root page.JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "which is responsible for the homepage, the starting page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 113.88,
          "en": "but we also have this nested page.JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.88,
          "end": 115.92,
          "en": "in this about folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.92,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "And that will be responsible for rendering the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 120.363,
          "en": "of the about route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.71,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "So it's now in here where we can export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 127.74,
          "en": "a new component function that could be called about page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.74,
          "end": 130.05,
          "en": "though this name does not matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.05,
          "end": 131.703,
          "en": "it can be anything you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 136.29,
          "en": "And then you have to return the JSX code that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.29,
          "end": 139.023,
          "en": "in the end, should be rendered as page content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.4,
          "end": 142.66,
          "en": "So here we could say about us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.61,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "and then add more content if we wanted to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 148.8,
          "en": "and we'll get to that meals app soon enough,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.8,
          "end": 150.81,
          "en": "but for this demo and these basics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.81,
          "end": 152.703,
          "en": "let's stick to this simple page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.8,
          "end": 156.72,
          "en": "With that added and saved,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.72,
          "end": 160.07999999999998,
          "en": "if you now go to localhost:3000/about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.07999999999998,
          "end": 162.84300000000002,
          "en": "you therefore now see about us on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.55,
          "end": 167.28,
          "en": "And here, I'll now just wrap it into a main element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.28,
          "end": 170.433,
          "en": "for styling purposes like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 174.99,
          "en": "This ensures due to the styles I set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.99,
          "end": 176.493,
          "en": "that this will be centered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 182.25,
          "en": "So that is how we can add a new route by adding a folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.25,
          "end": 184.893,
          "en": "with a page.JS file inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
